  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n   - Central idea: employ adaptive resolution optimization to minimize the overlap integral\n   - Steps: 1. Maintain the parent's integrity with step doubling/halving 2. Use local search (CMA-ES) to find better solutions 3. Evaluate solutions across multiple resolutions\n   - Key advantages: preserves core structure while enabling flexibility\n   - Constraints: all solutions must satisfy [0,1] bounds, fixed integral\n   - Potential performance risk: halving might dominate due to constraints\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n   - Objective: minimize C5 = max_k (1/dx * max_lag(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")[lag]))\n   - Variables: n_point grid points, each h[i] \u2208 [0,1] with sum(h)=n_points/2\n   - Feasibility: ensure both box constraints and integral constraint\n   - Score calculation: compute normalized correlation array using FFT-mode'full' for speed\n   - Optimization strategy: simulate Nelder-Mead on bounded box, restarts with coarse/fine resolution\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   - Initialize from parent if available (45 samples)\n   - Calculate solution based on integer log\u2082(n_points) to cover expansions from power-of-2 sizes\n   - Keep solutions valid by trilinear interpolation between finest grid available\n   - For each accordion point (n_points \u2208 nearest_valid_size), do:\n        * O(n_points) clean copied node generation\n        * Simplex optimization via Nelder-Mead projector\n        * Maintain best seen value\n        * Score evaluation via np.correlate(':full')\n   - Feasibility restoration via constraint projection is not needed for simplex-valid solutions\n\n4. Search Choices:\n   - Resolution transition: standardized halving procedure ensures reachable grid sizes\n   - Initial construction: stepvector generation based on current resolution\n   - Optimization parameters: all simplex dimensions fixed, bounded by [0,1] using projection of entire simplex\n\n5. Budget and Robustness:\n   - Time estimation: O(quantization_factor * resolution)\n   - Schedule: quantify resolution level; ascend if leaves time above minimum; tlim estimated via rule-of-thumb\n   - Failure: solution reverts to seed-safe candidate from evaluation history\n   - Limitations: may miss non-recipient optima\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n   - Check values are within [0,1] via simplex structure\n   - Check finite C5 via direct calculation\n   - Format: [h_array, c5_value, n_points]\n   - Error handling: if n_points not valid, revert to power-of-2 nearest without optimization",
